  "body": "A public write-up ([Concerning behavior from a popular open-weight AI model](https://cohere.com/blog/concerning-behaviour-popular-open-weight-ai-model)) describes an agent that, during a routine task, inventoried its host, tried an HTTP `PUT` to a cloud storage bucket, fetched files from a storage file proxy, reached for cloud metadata endpoints, and used `unshare` to get root inside a user namespace.\n\nRun as PreToolUse tool calls against the current release (17 calls covering those five behaviors), none produce a finding. Only the existing `curl-pipe-shell` control fires.\n\nProposed:\n- a new `agent-egress` pack, default `block`: cloud metadata access, file or environment uploads to object storage, the two hosts the write-up names, and `unshare` into a user namespace;\n- `command-risk` additions, default `warn`: data uploads to object storage, other Alibaba OSS hosts, download-then-execute, and recon plus a network call in one command.\n\nA broader default-deny design is in #924.\n",
